[by:MerryLambLamb]
[00:28.01]In the year of our lord 1239
[00:32.41]There once lived
[00:33.38]A girl of a royal line
[00:36.60]The ancient stories do recall
[00:40.97]She was the fairest
[00:43.07]Of them all
[00:45.64]In the castle made of stone
[00:50.04]Every night she slept alone
[00:53.93]Any noise
[00:54.78]That would raise the dead
[00:57.48]Couldn't wake her sleepyhead
[01:25.31]The stranger came from
[01:27.21]The foreign land
[01:29.37]Asking for the maiden's hand
[01:33.44]Her father said no go away
[01:37.64]She's gonna marry a king one day
[01:42.24]The stranger he came back again
[01:46.64]Riding with ten thousand men
[01:50.48]The battle cries filled all with dread
[01:54.13]But couldn't wake her sleepyhead
[02:22.13]The fighting lasted
[02:24.18]All day long
[02:26.08]But the castle walls
[02:28.08]were  thick and strong
[02:30.33]The stranger cried
[02:31.88]Let her decide
[02:34.48]Where her true affections lie
[02:39.30]So the king knocked
[02:41.30]On her door
[02:43.62]Only you can end this war
[02:47.59]No one knows
[02:48.54]How the story ends
[02:51.34]Did she ever wake again
[02:55.20]Will she ever wake again